This repository holds build recipes for packages of other people's software. The software itself is not
part of it: sources are downloaded when a package is built, and the built packages are not kept here.
The recipes written here are licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE).

The following third-party material is included and keeps its own license.

packaging/curl/debian/ and packaging/kitty/debian/
  Debian and Ubuntu's packaging of curl and kitty, adapted here (patches added or dropped, the
  rules changed). The copyright and license of each file are given in debian/copyright of each tree and in
  the headers of the files in debian/patches/. In short:
    curl   - upstream: Daniel Stenberg and many contributors, under the curl license;
             debian/: the Debian curl maintainers and Ubuntu developers.
    kitty  - upstream: Kovid Goyal, GPL-3+; debian/: James McCoy and Maytham Alsudany, with Ubuntu's changes.
  The kitty patches 0016 and 0017 written here change kitty's own source and follow kitty's license (GPL-3).

Symbols Nerd Font Mono (SymbolsNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf) in the kitty package
  Neither the font nor its license documents are kept in this repository. packaging/kitty/build.sh takes the
  font out of kitty's own signed release archive when a package is built, so it is the Nerd Fonts version that
  upstream kitty ships (v3.3.0 for kitty 0.49.2), finds the Nerd Fonts release it comes from, and fetches that
  release's license documents, which the package installs next to the font (/usr/lib/kitty/fonts/):
    LICENSE                      MIT, Copyright (c) 2014 Ryan L McIntyre (the Symbols Only release asset)
    NERD-FONTS-LICENSE           the repository's LICENSE, with the SIL OFL 1.1 text
    NERD-FONTS-LICENSE-AUDIT.md  the licenses of the glyph sets the font gathers
    NERD-FONTS-VERSION           which Nerd Fonts release the font is
  Nerd Fonts, https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts, states the license of the Symbols Only font as MIT.
  The glyph sets inside it keep their own licenses (for v3.3.0: Codicons and Font Awesome CC-BY-4.0, Material
  Design Icons Apache-2.0, Pomicons and Weather Icons OFL-1.1, several MIT, Powerline Symbols "Free License",
  Font Logos unlicensed); packaging/kitty/debian/copyright lists them.

Go code linked into kitty's Go programs (kitten): the Go modules in kitty's vendor/ (36 for kitty 0.49.2) and
  the Go standard library. Their code is not in this repository. When the kitty package is built,
  packaging/kitty/gen-vendor-licenses.py copies each module's license files into the package
  (/usr/share/doc/kitty/vendor-licenses/) and writes a paragraph for each into the package's copyright file.

